Hatr aims to replace the existing Job System with a cloud native design that will allow people to easily build async operations.

It should be easy to develop for and offer an out the box retyring mechanism in at attempt to offer guaranteed eventual consistency.  

The Hatr is targeted to be running in staging by January 2023.


Early demo of usage: [https://trebu-my.sharepoint.com/:v:/g/personal/skhan\_trebu\_co/EV0sTUBwSrpHkBaFNumBsLsBWW1aoAPWurfdYLAKW0mjzQ](https://trebu-my.sharepoint.com/:v:/g/personal/skhan_trebu_co/EV0sTUBwSrpHkBaFNumBsLsBWW1aoAPWurfdYLAKW0mjzQ)

## Architecture 


## Model, Task and Steps

A Hatr task is comprised of 3 elements.

1. Model
    1. This contains all the parameters required to execute the work.
    2. All elements in the Task use the same model.
    3. The model is saved after every step, allowing retries to pickup where we left off.
2. Task
    1. This defines what Model and Steps should be used to execute the work.
    2. Tasks have a Version and offer the ability to upgrade older Models if a breaking change is introduced.
3. Steps
    1. A Task can be made up of 1 to many Steps.
    2. A Step should be a small single retryable unit of the work.
    3. It’s advised to try and break your work up into smaller natural Steps. 

#### Model

```c
public class ExampleModel : HatrModel
{
    [JsonPropertyName("t")]
    public string TextToPrint { get; set; }

    public ExampleModel(string textToPrint)
    {
        this.TextToPrint = textToPrint;
    }
}
```

#### Task

```c
public class ExampleTask : HatrTask<ExampleModel>
{
    /// <inheritdoc />
    public override ushort Version => 2;

    /// <inheritdoc />
    protected override HatrStep<ExampleModel>[] GetSteps()
    {
        // I would of preferred to make this fully generic inside the class definition
        // but that becomes quite hard to understand.
        // Here you return all the instantiated classes of steps you want to run
        // BUT PLEASE DON'T PUT ANY LOGIC INSIDE THEIR CONSTRUCTOR'S
        return new HatrStep<ExampleModel>[]
        {
            new ExampleStep1(),
            new ExampleStep2(),
        };
    }

    /// <inheritdoc />
    protected override bool TryMigrateModel(ExampleModel model, ushort modelVersion, HatrContext context)
    {
        // Example
        switch (modelVersion)
        {
            case 1 :
            {
                // Migrate version 1 of the Task Model to Version 2
                model.TextToPrint = $"Migrated from Version 1 {model.TextToPrint}";

                // Return true saying we have migrated it and it's safe to run
                return true;
            }
        }

        // Return false indicating we don't know how to migrate the older version
        return false;
    }
}
```

#### Steps

```c
public class ExampleStep1 : HatrStep<ExampleModel>
{
    /// <inheritdoc />
    protected override async Task Execute(ExampleModel model, HatrContext context)
    {
        Console.WriteLine("Example Step 1");
        Console.WriteLine(DateTime.Now);
        Console.WriteLine(model.TextToPrint);

        Random rnd = new Random(DateTime.Now.Millisecond);
        if (rnd.NextDouble() < 0.5d)
        {
            throw new Exception("Flipped a coin and lost.");
        }
    }

    /// <inheritdoc />
    protected override async Task OnComplete(ExampleModel model, HatrContext context)
    {
        Console.WriteLine("Example Step 1 : Complete");
    }

    /// <inheritdoc />
    protected override async Task<HatrOnFailBehaviour> OnFail(ExampleModel model, HatrContext context)
    {
        Console.WriteLine("Example Step 1 : Fail");

        return HatrOnFailBehaviour.RetryStepExecute;
    }

    /// <inheritdoc />
    protected override async Task OnFinally(ExampleModel model, HatrContext context)
    {
        Console.WriteLine("Example Step 1 : Finally");
    }
}
```

